  "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
  "scope": "Only Table 1 (Swine) and Table 2 (Chickens) are imported. FeedSport formulates pigs and broiler chickens only; the cattle, sheep, goat, horse, rabbit, fish and turkey tables are deliberately not imported.",
  "basis": "Values are expressed based on the total diet at 88% dry matter (as fed basis) (Table 1 note 1, Table 2 note 2). They apply to the total diet, not to individual ingredients.",
  "feedsportUse": "Advisory upper-limit references only. FeedSport compares every value with the total-diet concentration of the recipe; none is an optimiser constraint and none decides whether a recipe meets its hard requirements.",
  "sourceAnomalies": [
    {
      "id": "swine-range-notation",
      "table": "Table 1: Swine",
      "description": "Three column headers are printed as \"7 to -11 kg\", \"11 to -25 kg\" and \"50 to -75 kg\". FeedSport reads them as 7 to 11 kg, 11 to 25 kg and 50 to 75 kg, the reading consistent with the neighbouring columns."
    },
    {
      "id": "chicken-starter-age",
      "table": "Table 2: Chickens",
      "description": "The Starter column is printed as \"0 to 8 weeks\" while the Grower column is \"4 to 8 weeks\", so the two overlap. Every nutrient value in the two columns is identical, so the overlap never changes a maximum. FeedSport assigns broiler phases that end by day 28 to Starter and later phases to Grower, using the Grower column's 4-week start as the boundary."
    }
  ],
